  "body": "## Summary\n\nSlice 2 of issue #5766 (deploy tool v1), building on slice 1 (PR #6231, merged: `deployTargets` registry + `deploy list` + definition validation). Queue task 13021.\n\nWhat lands in `pkgs/deploy/deploy.py`:\n\n- **Systemd unit rendering** (`render_unit`) and a **launchd plist stub** (`render_plist`) from a registry definition. The rendered `ExecStart` / program path points at the service's per-service nix profile `current` link (`/nix/var/nix/profiles/per-service/<name>/current/<entryPoint>`, design §4.1) — never at a bare store path — so a generation flip is a profile repoint and the rendered file is identical for every generation of the same definition. systemd argument/environment quoting escapes whitespace, quotes, backslashes, and doubles the `%`/`$` introducers.\n- **`deploy <target> --dry-run`**: the ordered §4.1 activation plan (build → install next generation into the profile → write unit/plist → daemon-reload → restart only that unit → health check → flip back on failure → append to the generation log), with no side effects.\n- **Generation log** (design §4.6): append-only JSONL per target under the state dir (`--state-dir` / `$DEPLOY_STATE_DIR`), one record per activation event carrying generation id, source rev, artifact, timestamp, actor, action, result. Logs are never truncated (two generations always retained).\n- **`deploy <target> status`**: folds the log into current/previous generations (a rollback event makes the generation it repointed to current) and reports the health verdict for the target's `healthCheck` URL, or that no check is defined.\n- **`rollback` command logic**: selects the previous *distinct* generation (repointing, never rebuilding) and is refused when fewer than two distinct generations were ever current.\n- Real activation — `nix-env` profile install, `systemctl` restart, health-check flip-back — is the next slice: the non-dry-run deploy/rollback paths say so explicitly and exit non-zero rather than pretending to have activated something. The remaining on-laptop E2E acceptance from issue #5766 also stays open there.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `pkgs/deploy/test_deploy_slice2.py` (21 tests, stdlib unittest): unit/plist rendering invariants, generation-log round-trip/fold/rollback-fold, plan ordering and flip-back step, rollback refusal cases, status formatting, and CLI subprocess cases (dry-run creates no state, real deploy refused, seeded-log status, unknown target). Oracle: design §4.1/§4.2/§4.6 + the issue text, named in the test module docstring.\n- New flake check `deploy-slice2-tests` in `lib/default.nix` next to `deploy-dupkeys-property`, running the new test file against `deploy.py` in CI.\n- Existing coverage re-verified locally on the laptop against the new `deploy.py`: `test_dupkeys_property.py` (300 cases, property holds), `deploy list` on a valid registry, malformed registry rejected with field-level errors, `status` on an empty log.\n\nRefs #5766 (issue stays open for the activation slice + E2E acceptance).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796735285&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7692&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7692&signature=12773fdf90913a79c9c6d771dbbea103a14632a18ce0cf15f2e6b83390b0b612\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7692?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
